sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Adjuster (human)
    participant C as Claims Agent Client
    participant AS as Authorization Server :8000
    participant M as Claims MCP Server :8001

    C->>M: POST /mcp initialize (no token)
    M-->>C: 401 WWW-Authenticate: resource_metadata=...
    C->>M: GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp
    M-->>C: authorization_servers: [":8000"]
    C->>AS: GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
    AS-->>C: endpoints + S256 PKCE required

    Note over C: generate code_verifier + code_challenge (S256)

    C->>A: open browser -> /authorize?...&code_challenge=...
    A->>AS: GET /authorize (consent screen)
    AS-->>A: show requested scopes (claims.read, policy.read, claims.review, claims.adjudicate)
    A->>AS: POST /authorize decision=allow
    AS-->>C: 302 redirect to loopback callback ?code=...&state=...

    Note over C: verify state matches (CSRF check)

    C->>AS: POST /token code + code_verifier
    AS->>AS: verify_pkce(code_verifier, code_challenge)
    AS-->>C: access_token (JWT, 5min TTL) + refresh_token

    C->>M: POST /mcp tools/call get_claim (Bearer JWT)
    M->>M: verify signature via JWKS + aud + iss + exp
    M->>M: wall #1: scope includes claims.read?
    M-->>C: claim file

    C->>M: POST /mcp tools/call review_claim_decision
    M->>M: wall #1: scope includes claims.review?
    M->>M: wall #2: AI-assist queue? claim type allowed? amount <= authority?
    M-->>C: review_id (TTL 300s), summary

    C->>A: show summary, wait for confirmation
    A->>C: types YES

    C->>M: POST /mcp tools/call submit_claim_decision (review_id, idempotency_key)
    M->>M: wall #1: scope includes claims.adjudicate?
    M->>M: review_id single-use? not expired? owner matches sub claim?
    M->>M: wall #2 re-checked against frozen review
    M-->>C: finalized decision_id

    C->>M: retry submit_claim_decision (same idempotency_key)
    M-->>C: same decision_id, idempotent=true
